      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F=(2x+3y-4z)^{2}\\,i+(2x+3y-4z)^{2}\\,j+(2x+3y-4z)^{2}\\,k.$ \nFind $∇\\cdot F.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((2x+3y-4z)^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}((2x+3y-4z)^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((2x+3y-4z)^{2}) \\\\  & =4(2x+3y-4z)+6(2x+3y-4z)-8(2x+3y-4z) \\\\  & =2(2x+3y-4z) \\\\  & =4x+6y-8z.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
